 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [SDF Underlay & Inner Underlay](5612-sdf-underlay-inner-underlay.md)
-Renders a blurred, colored border either behind (underlay) or inside (inner underlay) the primary glyph face. It differs by offsetting the UV sampling in the SDF atlas and blending with the face color, allowing for "inner" outlines that appear within the character fill. Choose this when you need decorative or depth-indicating borders that are not strictly part of the glyph's stroke geometry.
+Renders a blurred, colored border either behind (underlay) or inside (inner underlay) the primary glyph face. It differs from standard outline methods by allowing the border to be offset in UV space independently of the glyph geometry and by supporting "inner" rendering where the border appears within the filled region of the character. Choose this when you need decorative or depth-indicating borders that are not strictly part of the glyph's stroke geometry.
+
+### Multi-Smoke Layer Compositing
+A compositing technique that blends up to 8 smoke layers by iteratively selecting the nearest smoke layer based on depth texture and blending it with the accumulated color [S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard layered compositing by dynamically resolving layer order via depth comparison rather than fixed layer indices [S2, unofficial]. Choose this when rendering volumetric smoke with multiple overlapping density layers where depth ordering is critical [S2, unofficial].
 
